DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The bbiinnttiimmee() and ggeettbbiinnttiimmee() functions store the system time as a
     _s_t_r_u_c_t _b_i_n_t_i_m_e at the addresses specified by _b_t.  The mmiiccrroottiimmee() and
     ggeettmmiiccrroottiimmee() functions perform the same utility, but record the time as
     a _s_t_r_u_c_t _t_i_m_e_v_a_l instead.  Similarly the nnaannoottiimmee() and ggeettnnaannoottiimmee()
     functions store the time as a _s_t_r_u_c_t _t_i_m_e_s_p_e_c.

     The bbiinnttiimmee(), mmiiccrroottiimmee(), and nnaannoottiimmee() functions always query the
     timecounter to return the current time as precisely as possible.  Whereas
     ggeettbbiinnttiimmee(), ggeettmmiiccrroottiimmee(), and ggeettnnaannoottiimmee() functions are abstrac‐
     tions which return a less precise, but faster to obtain, time.

     The intent of the ggeettbbiinnttiimmee(), ggeettmmiiccrroottiimmee(), and ggeettnnaannoottiimmee() func‐
     tions is to enforce the user's preference for timer accuracy versus exe‐
     cution time.

